{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02200",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 5.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Ah, hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.66,
      "end_seconds": 9.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.69,
      "end_seconds": 17.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "So the thing is, you know, I've got dark urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.72,
      "end_seconds": 21.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.84,
      "end_seconds": 24.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Nothing regular, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.15,
      "end_seconds": 29.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.09,
      "end_seconds": 38.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Probably about two weeks. Yeah. Um, I've also been feeling sick, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.76,
      "end_seconds": 44.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "And what about confusion, high fever or itching?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.53,
      "end_seconds": 50.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "No, no confusion, high fever or itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.54,
      "end_seconds": 54.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Alright, any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.36,
      "end_seconds": 60.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.97,
      "end_seconds": 68.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.86,
      "end_seconds": 73.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.69,
      "end_seconds": 87.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.18,
      "end_seconds": 98.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Erm, I have high blood pressure, for about ten years. I've been reading about it online and it worried me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.61,
      "end_seconds": 113.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.07,
      "end_seconds": 127.47,
      "duration_seconds": 13.4,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. No, I've never smoked in my life. I swim twice a week. I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.12,
      "end_seconds": 132.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.26,
      "end_seconds": 141.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.81,
      "end_seconds": 175.77,
      "duration_seconds": 15.96,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 124 over 78, pulse is 84 beats a minute. And height 180 centimetres, temp 36.9 degrees, weight 71 kilos, SpO2 99 percent on room air, BMI works out to 21.9."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.17,
      "end_seconds": 178.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.83,
      "end_seconds": 184.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.16,
      "end_seconds": 189.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.81,
      "end_seconds": 208.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Yes, uh, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.16,
      "end_seconds": 211.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.97,
      "end_seconds": 224.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "The whites of the eyes are yellow and the liver edge is tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.62,
      "end_seconds": 228.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Yes, um, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.24,
      "end_seconds": 233.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.25,
      "end_seconds": 254.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, my working impression is acute hepatitis, possibly hepatitis A after travel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.45,
      "end_seconds": 260.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.25,
      "end_seconds": 292.5,
      "duration_seconds": 31.25,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with acute hepatitis, possibly hepatitis A after travel do well once it's treated properly. I'll request an ultrasound of the liver, it'll help with jaundice. I want liver blood tests done, that's for jaundice. Rest, avoid alcohol and wash your hands carefully, as it can spread. If it hasn't settled in a month, we'd think about a hepatitis screen, but not now. See me again in one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.08,
      "end_seconds": 296.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Okay, I'll arrange it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.78,
      "end_seconds": 301.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.92,
      "end_seconds": 305.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Well, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.55,
      "end_seconds": 307.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}